     "rate": "+0%",
     "text": "Wall Street floors run on flashing screens while high speed trades fire every millisecond. You think financial markets are just chaotic gambling halls where lucky speculators place wild bets, but they are organized arenas. Buyers and sellers meet here to transact in financial assets and contracts, setting every price through direct interaction. Companies or governments issue brand new bonds directly to investors in the primary market. Once those assets are issued, they move straight to the secondary market where investors trade them endlessly. These systems rely entirely on informational transparency to allocate capital efficiently across the whole economy."
